workplan/2026-10-12-simplification-workplan.md:5:**Basis:** the stage graph (`workplan/pipeline-state-graph/`: `STATE-GRAPH.md`, `CONFLICTS.md`, `CAPABILITIES.md`, `build_graph.py`), measured on 2026-10-12 and 2026-10-13. **Compared with the ideal state graph** (`IDEAL-GRAPH.md`, a clean-sheet design, partly withdrawn after an antagonist pass) in `COMPARISON.md`; **the open questions are ruled in `RULINGS.md`** (R1–R42 delivered under LED-154 on the owner's commission, R43–R49 the 2026-10-14 resolutions; effective by the ledger entry "Owner delegation 2026-10-14"). **The slices listed in §5a were rehearsed** in scratch clones of `31142552` and stacked (the reports are in `workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/`); steps 0.3 to 0.6, Phase 2, R37, 3.R, Phase 4 and Phase 5 were not, and the walkability of the whole graph, in every direction, is measured in `WALKABILITY.md` with `walkability.py`. Figures are results of the command beside them, of a command in §9, or of the report cited, unless marked *estimate*; a few counts taken from records (the 151 attestations, the 458-row ledger, the 188 decision rows, the 13 status corrections, "about 110 lines") have no command beside them: re-derive before quoting (CLAUDE.md rule 7a). **Rulings are `RULINGS.md` numbers (R1–R42); the plan's own working rules are W1–W10 (§3)**, and the rehearsal reports, written against v3.3, cite the working rules as R1–R9.
workplan/2026-10-12-simplification-workplan.md:39:- **Walkability.** The owner's requirement is handshakes in every direction (down, up, lateral, cross-stage skip, re-entrant) and walkability across every table that carries an id or reference. `IDEAL-GRAPH.md` §6 measures up and down: 21 of 82 tables fail today. `workplan/pipeline-state-graph/walkability.py` measures all five directions, declared and populated (`WALKABILITY.md`). The verdict there is no: after Phase 1 nothing reaches render, synthesis does not point at judgment, research reaches the later stages only through `evidence_sources`, and one parameter of ten and one slug of 106 reach an extraction. Phase 1 as rehearsed deletes 45 foreign keys, of which 4 hold pointers (all in the two axis maps R3 retires), and adds none.
workplan/2026-10-12-simplification-workplan.md:159:| G (`rehearsals/G-r18-lens.md`) | R18 | EXECUTABLE WITH CHANGES | 14 files, +163/−60; W3 areas +62/−5; migration 16 lines; `P-M`, C1.8 PASS; `--all` 63 → 65 green | The key of `access_needs` is `need_code`; the view name collides with the `v_coverage_*` family and the ideal's counting rule counts deferrals as searches; the writer change is +17 lines, not "unsized"; the step stales two freshness checks unless 1.1 has landed; it replaces no code |
workplan/2026-10-12-simplification-workplan.md:185:| **judgment** | **Stage-map (R32):** `source_value_extractions` and `extraction_relations` move to judgment (C-012; owner words LED-106 as adopted, LED-108); CLAUDE.md §3's row that puts "extraction" at evidence is corrected (owner merge). **This is the move that makes judgment a stage in the walk:** under the live map no foreign key has a judgment table as parent, and with the move `specification_extraction_links.extraction_id` gives judgment a populated (151-row) pointer to specification and evidence a fourth pointer into judgment (`WALKABILITY.md` §2). The crossing is judgment's output, written on the extraction's lens columns, never presupposed and never defaulted (R33, LED-113). **Scan contract (R37):** delete the slug-admission refusal in `insert_extraction` once T1 has landed (the scan contract says slugs guide search only); `source_slug_links` stays as the admission record; `source_value_extractions.slug` is writer-retired and NULL-forwarded, which needs a rebuild of that table (`NOT NULL REFERENCES slugs(slug)`): **do it in the same rebuild as the root pointer, so the table is rebuilt once.** T1's scan contract governs (`COMPARISON.md` P12): `source_scans` and `v_scan_ledger` are a separate ledger and add no column to `source_value_extractions`; the ideal's `scan_id` NOT NULL with a composite foreign key is not adopted. **Root pointer (R24).** One schema migration, numbered at merge, rebuilds `source_value_extractions` with `root_id TEXT REFERENCES external_root_registry(root_id)`, nullable, by the 081 procedure: (1) save `sqlite_sequence` to a temp table; (2) drop the views that read the table, re-derived at execution as the transitive closure over `sqlite_master` (six on 2026-10-13: `v_root_id_conflicts`, `v_derived_figure_check`, `v_determination_provenance`, `v_unregistered_roots`, `v_scan_ledger`, `v_value_independence`); (3) create the new table from the live DDL, changing only the `root_id` line, and `INSERT … SELECT` every column by name; (4) drop the old table and rename the new one; (5) recreate the five indexes and the views verbatim from their stored SQL; (6) restore the sequence. The four child tables need no edit. Declare `-- AFTER_DATA: <latest data migration>` (W6): 25 data migrations INSERT into the table and 12 UPDATE it, but no committed migration writes a `root_id`, so the marker records the chronology and is not load-bearing today. `insert_extraction` refuses an unregistered `--root-id` in words (+9 lines; a W3 exception that replaces none). **Same PR (decided, R49(d)):** the key makes `root_id` registry-only, which supersedes the sentence of `governance/evidence-architecture.md` (a) (and DR-2026-07-13 H1's "in corpus" reading); write the `SUPERSEDES`/`BY` pair in the ledger and amend (a) in the same change (`supersession_backpointer_audit` requires the target document to carry the pointer), and update atom EVI-162, or the audit and `build_graph.py --check` fail. **File the registry's writer as a GAP** (rule 10): a minted id, a non-blank description that refuses a normalised duplicate, `root_type` from the CHECK, provenance as a pointer, a refusal for in-corpus roots; until it exists the pointer is declared and unpopulated. **Done when:** every view selects with unchanged counts and verbatim SQL (four of the six return 0 rows, so the SQL, not the count, is the proof); `--rebuild` is identical including `sqlite_sequence`; the walkability script drops `external_root_registry` and `source_value_extractions` from its failing set. Measured: migration 366 lines (an 8-line `writable_schema` variant exists; SQLite documents it for removing constraints, so it is not recommended without the owner's acceptance). | `P-STAGE-SVE`, `P-V2`, C1.4 |
workplan/2026-10-12-simplification-workplan.md:187:| **specification** | **T3-grey alone (R9):** band only; the engine's `pending` stands (C-004). `determination_gates` carries `identity_code` only: add the lens columns, or point at the determination (rule 5); decide after a `repo-sweep` of its readers. **The determination's marker** (`COMPARISON.md` P18; R7, R39). One tooling PR. *Migration:* `ALTER TABLE specifications ADD COLUMN marker` (not a table rebuild: the AUTOINCREMENT sequence, 065's lens CHECK, the three inbound foreign keys, `idx_spec_row_identity`, `trg_spec_retire_needs_reason` and the seven views stay untouched) with two column CHECKs — `marker IS NULL OR (marker IN ('●','◐','○') AND (regulatory_stratum_only = 0 OR marker = '○'))` and `retired_at IS NOT NULL OR (state IN ('stated','provisional')) = (marker IS NOT NULL)` — and `-- AFTER_DATA: <latest data migration>` (SQLite checks an added CHECK against existing rows; 095's marker already orders it after every `specifications` write). It redefines `v_best_practice` without `strength_band`, a second two-valued band that has no code reader. *Engine, same PR:* `assess_cell.determine` computes the marker and `main` writes it: each governing source carries its §5 band and the cell takes their floor-mean; a value read off the regulatory stratum (floor claim or proxy threshold) is ○ unless a `confirms` edge from an anchoring finding reaches a governing extraction row, and then that code takes the confirming study's band (R39; it fires on 0 live edges, all three being `to_label`). `EvidenceStateRecord` gains `marker`. The four tests the fifth pass named supply a marker wherever they write or un-retire a live stated or provisional row (without it their refusal assertions pass vacuously); `test_assess_cell_pilot` asserts the bands, the CHECK and the owner's five-row floor-mean table. Regenerate `tools/pipeline-completeness-dashboard.html` and `tools/pipeline-walk.html` unless 1.1 has landed. *Owner merge:* the three prose callers of `strength_band` (`evidence-architecture.md` lines 119 and 206, keeping atom EVI-182's quoted phrase; `evidence-methodology.md` line 144) and the mission line. Rehearsed: 14 files, +208/−56 (code +79/−24, tests +79/−25, migration +44); `--rebuild` identical; no gate worse than baseline; **W3 exception: the step adds code (net +152) and replaces none; the column and the engine rule are new**. *Corrections to R7 and R9 found by implementing them:* R7's "Option A §3" is DR-2026-07-21 §2.3; it omits the owner's 2026-09-13 floor-of-the-mean rulings and LED-020; it does not cover the proxy determination (○ unless confirmed, by the 2026-09-13 upgrade ruling); R9's engine line `:1510` is the H4 cap, and "parity inside the weak band" is false for T3-grey (three converging T3-grey sources stay `pending`). *Not built:* the band of a `figure_role='derived'` row (0 rows); a T3-clinical confirming study (the CHECK pins the cell at ○); `derivation_sha` does not cover `extraction_relations`, so a later `confirms` edge leaves a stale marker under an unchanged sha. ◐ never appears on a determination the engine writes today. | `P-GT`, `P-ENG-T3` |
workplan/2026-10-12-simplification-workplan.md:188:| **render** | **3.R** One renderer (target at most 300 lines) over **one view to be built**: no view today carries the marker or a strength flag, because that logic lives in `pilot_renderings.py` (`REGISTER_MAP`, `ROLES`, `tuple_class`), which 1.1 deletes, and all 8 live `specifications` rows are retired, so a view over live determinations returns 0 rows until a determination is written. The marker has one home, `specifications.marker`; `v_best_practice` carries it through `SELECT *` and the view to be built reads it, so the band half of the register invariants holds by construction (the CHECK refuses a regulatory-stratum-only row above ○ and a live stated or provisional row without a marker) and `register_integrity_check` has nothing left to check. What the renderer still owns is the weak/code-derived flag text and the register map, and rendering `provisional ●` (T3-clinical-only, or an H4-capped cell) distinctly from `stated ●`. The view filters on `superseded_by_ref_id IS NULL` wherever it joins a source. **The probe measures it only if the view reads a table mapped to render** (a view's stages are those of the tables it reads): after Phase 1 render is one orphan table with no pointer to or from any stage, so the walk into render exists only as that view; name a render-mapped table for it to read, or extend the probe to map views (`WALKABILITY.md` §7, finding 1). **Probe P-K scans a hard-coded tuple of renderer paths** (`build_graph.py`, probe P-K); the renderer's path is added to that tuple in this step's PR, or P-K stays NOT-BUILT over a live renderer. The 300-line target is an estimate until the view exists. A named exception to W3: it replaces 1.1's renderers. | `P-K`, C4.6, C4.8 |
workplan/2026-10-12-simplification-workplan.md:197:| **4.4** | **One derived walkability check.** The script in `IDEAL-GRAPH.md` §6 (about 40 lines; 21 of 82 fail on the live schema) becomes the registered check that fails on any table that is unmapped, orphaned, dangling or unreachable toward base or the determination, outside two named residuals (LED-083 reservations; infrastructure). It replaces `graph_audit`, `test_graph_audit` and the `scripts/audit/graph/` modules, which 1.2 to 1.3 have already edited (`wc -l scripts/audit/graph/*.py scripts/audit/graph_audit.py`; `schema_reference_audit` skips `scripts/audit/graph/` by path, and that skip goes with them; also `db_path_env_audit.py` (its `EXEMPT` entry for `graph_audit.py`) and the three fixture exemptions in `governance/schema-reference-exemptions.yaml`; `COMPARISON.md` P20). Net negative; it is the owner's "walkability across all tables with references and ids". **It is registered only when the set it prints is empty or every member is a named residual:** 15 of 56 tables fail it on the rehearsed stack (21 of 82 today; `rehearsals/STACK.md`; the failing set is row-bearing orphans awaiting LED-169 rulings and the follow-the-ruling tables), and a check that is red from the day it lands is the pattern rule 6 and the registry's own level text warn against. Until then it is a command whose output is the measure, and `graph_audit` stays. **The other directions are measured by `workplan/pipeline-state-graph/walkability.py`** (receiving and sending foreign keys per stage pair, lateral components, skip, re-entrant, zigzag, declared against populated pointers; `WALKABILITY.md`): scaffolding that leaves with the instrument in Phase 6 unless the owner keeps it, run at the end of each phase and at the end of the plan as the measure of "walkable in all directions". It is not a registered check. |
workplan/2026-10-12-simplification-workplan.md:198:| **4.5** | **Centralize bindings** (`COMPARISON.md` P21). One binding each for the database path, the repository root and the clock in `dbcore`, passed down as arguments; replace the per-file bindings (the ideal counts 69 files reading `GUIDEBOOK_DB_PATH` and 58 `REPO_ROOT` definitions: `IDEAL-GRAPH.md` §8) one file at a time, deleting each as it goes. Behaviour-preserving; the done-when is the ideal's [cR16] list shrinking. |
workplan/2026-10-12-simplification-workplan.md:202:Only research rows remain. PR #171 already put batch 24 on `main`. Owed from its body: a compensating data migration using T1's `annotate-parameter`, because the note on all nine parameters is false for parameter 12 and restates facts the schema derives (rule 3 forbids editing the first migration). Per the medical-lens ruling (R16), the medical-registry rows through `add-medical`, filled by correspondence from persisted WHO payloads; until then `log-search --medical` and the medical lens column refuse or stay NULL. **T1's `scan_debt` (advisory) reports the (source, parameter) pairs not yet read** (468 when T1 landed in the rehearsal): that is this phase's work or a baseline entry, and the PR that lands T1 says which. **The legacy bytes backlog** (`COMPARISON.md` P11, P24): the sources with no persisted payload (15 of 53 are keyed on no manifest line and 11 are named in no manifest at all, re-derived 2026-10-12 over `ref_id`, `ref_id_note` and any `REF-` text; payload quality is a separate count) re-retrieved through `retrieval_log.fetch`, and `source_type` supplied for the 25 sources that lack it. **Rows the walk found missing** (`WALKABILITY.md` §6): two VERIFIED code sources with no admission row (`REF-00987`, `REF-01010`), seven early executions (ids 1 to 16, August 2026) whose `results_admitted` counts (10) predate the `search_admissions` rows, which begin at execution 30, 40 candidates with a NULL `exec_id`: record each admission through the verb or record why not. Research acts, so they ship here and not with the tooling. Once the bytes-pointer design exists (R23) and the backlog is empty, a last tooling migration makes its pointers NOT NULL, which is the ideal's constraint. `research_batch_dod.py` on `scratchpad/CURRENT`. Open last; unsubscribe.
workplan/2026-10-23-pipeline-resolution-workplan.md:41:| 4.4 one derived walkability check | no commit names it | after T-5, if its registration condition can be met. It registers the table-level check of IDEAL-GRAPH §6 (per table: reaches base, reaches the determination, orphan, dangling), **not** a stage-pair measure; its own text says `walkability.py` "is not a registered check". It registers only when the set it prints is empty or every member is a named residual, and until then `graph_audit` stays. So it is **not counted as an offset here**: it would delete `graph_audit.py`, `scripts/audit/graph/` and their test (`wc -l scripts/audit/graph_audit.py scripts/audit/graph/*.py scripts/tests/test_graph_audit.py`; the code alone was 1,385 lines on 2026-10-23) only once its condition is met. [UNVERIFIED: that the roughly 40-line check covers every duty of `graph_audit`; that is the old plan's claim.] |
