workplan/2026-10-23-pipeline-resolution-workplan.md:135:**T-5 Render** (report T-5, plan step 3.R). Needs T-2, T-3, T-4; OR-7, OR-11b. Resolves Q0, Q8 (render), E4 (the `insufficient` and `exceeds` edges only; see §9), E6, E7 (handoff), E10. Redefines `v_best_practice` (a T6-only cell appears, flagged), adds `v_determination_branches` and `v_code_inadequacy`, and adds `scripts/generate/render_cells.py`, which reads `specifications` directly so pending cells are not lost. Output goes to `$TMPDIR`; no rendered file is committed. **[Re-opened by the ruling on OW-1 (ledger, "Owner rulings 2026-10-29 (third)"): the render stage is expected to hold a table of complete prose and bibliographic information built from specifications and the preceding tables, so T-5's design waits on OW-1b and OW-1c.]**
workplan/2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages/HANDOFF.md:56:- **Best practice** = the best way to do something for the intended group. It is NOT the most common or most agreed value.
