workplan/2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages/RENDER-DECISIONS-AND-PIPELINE.md:135:1. **[CORRECTION: "D3 conflicts with the mission document and tier-system §5/§8" — changed to "largely already resolved on `main`".]** The first version took the export's handoff at its word. `governance/tier-system.md` §8 and `governance/mission-and-epistemics.md` §2 were amended on 2026-07-21 (owner directive, Option A) so that a T4–T6-only determination is stated as weak-band (○) "best practice as currently known", always flagged weak and code-derived. I did not find a "wall" sentence in the mission document; its section 2 title is "code consensus anchors it only at the weak band". What remained between the owner's statements and `main` was the marker and flag, not the right to name the gentlest code value best practice; the owner has since confirmed the ○ band and flag stay (ledger 2026-10-30 second).
