workplan/2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages/reports/spec-page-design-requirements-2026-10-29.md:215:1. Evidence-state rule says a cell with sparse evidence displays `[BEST-PRACTICE-PENDING]` with a gap link. The owner said rows that are "Not set" should not show. Current handling: no table row, a plain statement in Gaps. Confirm.
workplan/2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages/reports/spec-page-design-requirements-2026-10-29.md:216:2. Doctrine says tier 4 to 6 are a regulatory baseline "walled off from best-practice anchoring" and that a best-practice claim from standards alone is "in error" when it comes from convergence. The owner's rule (best practice is the most accommodating value stated by a current standard unless evidence improves on it) is implemented as a single-source gentlest value, marked evidence-based but provisional, with the basis stated. Confirm this is the intended reading and whether the marker should be inferred instead.
workplan/2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages/reports/spec-page-design-requirements-2026-10-29.md:233:- Standards as best practice: the owner decided that the gentlest value found in practice is best practice and that no academic study is required; the mission document's tier 4 to 6 wall is therefore superseded in practice and needs a decision record (D-DOCT).
