workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DECISION-CLOSURE.md:34:**After the thirteenth set (2026-11-14).** You answered the four things of `OWNER-SHEET-PLAIN.md`: OD-43 (any two kinds of evidence may agree; agreement is most common practice, not best practice) and OD-44 (A) are answered by you; OD-49 is narrowed to building use and indoor or outdoor; OD-53 is overtaken for provisions that are there or not; and OD-56 is registered, open, for a delegated and independently checked resolution (prompt 18). You then answered OD-56 yourself, "b": a provision that is there or not is listed, by pointer, in the determination of the element that should carry it (prompt 18). Ledger: `grep -n -F "Owner answers 2026-11-14 (thirteenth set)" references/project-standards.md`. Re-run the generator for the blocking set; do not read it from here.
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DECISION-CLOSURE.md:115:**OD-28: the words are on file.** All eight relayed sentences are messages of human origin in `transcripts/harness_db856d85/main.jsonl` of 2026-10-12 (`origin.kind` human; O1 and O3 as queued commands at 01:51:55 and 02:05:50 UTC, O2 at 01:54:09, O4 to O8 between 02:09:02 and 02:12:19). Differences from the relayed text in `workplan/pipeline-state-graph/IDEAL-GRAPH.md` line 11: O1 begins "use Opus to create an idealized …" (the relay drops "use Opus to"); O7 begins "yeah, and we need to ensure …" (the relay drops "yeah, and"); the others match apart from trailing spaces. To see them (enqueue and delivery lines of the main session, not sidechains): `python3 -I -c "import json;P=['use Opus to create','just be code architecture','wherever there is a conflict','strive to minimize','centralized where possible','the less hard coded','handshakes both','handshake ALL'];[print(d.get('timestamp'),d.get('type'),[p for p in P if p in l]) for l in open('transcripts/harness_db856d85/main.jsonl') for d in [json.loads(l)] if d.get('type') in ('user','queue-operation') and any(p in l for p in P) and 'tool_result' not in l and d.get('isSidechain') is not True]"`; the delivered O1 to O3 carry `"origin": {"kind": "human"}` (`grep -c -F '"kind": "human"' transcripts/harness_db856d85/main.jsonl` counts all such lines).
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DECISION-CLOSURE.md:212:**Answered by you, 2026-11-14:** "yes convergence is possible too, and it helps define most common practice (which isn't same as best practice)", recorded as `OD-43: agreement between any two kinds of evidence counts as convergence; convergence defines most common practice, which is not best practice`. The delegated limit to research and lived-experience evidence is superseded; the other conditions stand as the recorder's reading. **Refined by you the same day** (ledger: `grep -n -F "Owner statement 2026-11-14 — convergence means values coming together" references/project-standards.md`): convergence means values coming together, among any sources (codes alone too) and across tiers; the number of independent roots is shown beside it, not required for it; its weight is read from the tiers of the sources that agree; two groups of evidence on different values are a divergence that starts an investigation; values within 5% count as the same; ranges are included. Ledger: `grep -n -F "Owner answers 2026-11-14 (thirteenth set)" references/project-standards.md`. The text below is kept as it was put.
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS-2-REVIEW.md:196:**Plain-language question: fair.** One addition I would make for fairness to B: "The July rule's purpose was to stop a value resting only on codes from ever being shown as best practice. Under A that protection is kept by the separate codes-only mark, which already exists." Without it the reader cannot see why B was ever chosen.
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS-2-REVIEW.md:202:**(2) Rulings.** The three-level ruling (PS:2053: "Building types (eg residential, commercial), room types (eg kitchen, entry, bathroom), construction elements (eg door, door handle, window, floor) are what I wanted for that table"), "5 is three" (PS:2419), the key (2026-08-26, 2026-08-28), one value per cell (`CLAUDE.md` §4, owner 2026-11-06), OR-2 (PS:4616): read correctly; (a2), (a3) and (b1) are correctly found unavailable. **Two over-reaches.** (i) "seeded from the owner's two examples": the owner's words are examples ("eg"), and OR-17 ("Ensure that these phrases/names/aliases are all present in their prescribed jurisdiction/language. It is not acceptable for the model to generate its own phrases/names/aliases", PS:4713) and E1 (a concept first met outside English is named by the instrument's own phrase) require each building type to be minted from an instrument's own scope phrase, in its language. Seeding English labels from the owner's examples would mint names no instrument used, the English bias the 2026-11-06 rulings forbid. (ii) (b2)'s "and its parent within the level" is unruled: the recorded analysis of "5 is three" says the levels do not nest and cross-level edges are junctions (PS:2436 onwards); a parent inside the element level is a new design for T-060 to justify, not part of this resolution. The appeal to OD-01 as a pattern is to a delegated resolution, not an owner ruling; it is consistency, not authority.
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS-REVIEW.md:27:- **One best practice, jurisdictions beside it.** PS:4822: "our guidebook doesn't take positions. it just presents what appears to be the most accommodating/gentle best practice … so unless an academic article or some professional body improves upon germany's standard, that's identified as the best practice"; PS:4844: "an easy comparison master table where you just see what each jurisdiction has for the value". Both say what the resolution says. **Verified.**
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS-REVIEW.md:37:- Jurisdiction vocabulary is listed among the owner's subjects (`CLAUDE.md` §8, "jurisdiction"); a parent-coded sub-national entry is a provenance refinement within an in-scope country and is covered by the delegation of OD-01 by name. Acceptable once the roll-up sentence is removed.
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS-REVIEW.md:96:- **2026-10-30 (PS:4840, 4888):** "i want it to be coming from database directly in ideal world"; "simply PRESENTING information without claiming correctness myself". Quoted correctly. DR-2026-07-21's "we never adjudicate a correct path or conclusion" is cited by the ledger entry at PS:4892, as stated.
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS.md:52:- The owner asked for a per-jurisdiction comparison beside the value, not for per-jurisdiction values: "for ramp gradient, i want there to also be an easy comparison master table where you just see what each jurisdiction has for the value" (PS:4844); "our guidebook doesn't take positions. it just presents what appears to be the most accommodating/gentle best practice … unless an academic article or some professional body improves upon germany's standard, that's identified as the best practice" (PS:4822), which names one best practice drawn across jurisdictions.
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS.md:60:- C2 (legibility) favours (a)/(c): designers and policy makers in a given jurisdiction see their own figure in the comparison table and the best practice above it; a per-jurisdiction determination would show a reader as many "best practices" as there are codes, which the owner rejected in PS:4822.
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS.md:197:- The spine names synthesis as a stage (CLAUDE.md §3; owner 2026-08-27, "synthesize judgments"). Synthesis-stage tables already exist and a determination already points at one: `specifications.convergence_id REFERENCES convergence_assessment` (`select sql from sqlite_master where name='specifications'`); `governance/stage-map.yaml` maps `convergence_assessment`, `convergence_sources`, `connections`, `connection_targets`, `conflicts` to synthesis. `best_practice_synthesis` no longer exists as a table (`select name from sqlite_master where name='best_practice_synthesis'` returns nothing).
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS.md:282:- OW-1, owner 2026-10-29: "I expect the render table to be one where the specification table rows have been converted into complete prose, bibliographic information etc accordingly from the preceding tables such that it can be displayed properly on the website repository" (PS:4729). 2026-10-30: "i want it to be coming from database directly in ideal world" (PS:4840); "simply PRESENTING information without claiming correctness myself" (PS:4888); DR-2026-07-21: "we never adjudicate a correct path or conclusion" (cited PS:4892). 2026-08-27: no committed file is a render (CLAUDE.md §3).
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/DELEGATED-RESOLUTIONS.md:284:- Only Opus-class models write best-practice synthesis (CLAUDE.md §6). OR-6: the item's discussion notes a T2 dispute of a T1 value (PS:4626).
