workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/REMEDIATION-WORKPLAN.md:896:- **Status (2026-11-14): ANSWERED BY THE OWNER** — `OD-43: agreement between any two kinds of evidence counts as convergence; convergence defines most common practice, which is not best practice`. The owner's words (answer 1 of the thirteenth set): "yes convergence is possible too, and it helps define most common practice (which isn't same as best practice)". The delegated limit to the clinical and Co-1 axes is superseded on contact; the remaining conditions (same value or range, anchoring claims that can all hold, two or more independent roots) stand as the recorder's [ASSUMPTION]; a convergence output is most common practice and is never labelled or rendered as best practice. Ledger: `grep -n -F "Owner answers 2026-11-14 (thirteenth set)" references/project-standards.md`. **Blocks now:** nothing (T-068 still waits for T-059 to merge). **Read by:** T-068 (its "Owner decisions" bullet); the render note in T-037 and T-032. **Refined the same day (2026-11-14) by the owner's statements** (ledger: `grep -n -F "Owner statement 2026-11-14 — convergence means values coming together" references/project-standards.md`; the answer line stands, no new status line): convergence means values coming together, among any sources and across any tiers, codes alone included; the root count is shown beside every convergence, not required for it (the "two or more independent roots" condition above is withdrawn); significance is read from the converging sources' tiers and bands, never as a score; convergence is most common practice and moves no value or marker; two or more clusters on different values are divergence between sets and a cue to investigate; a 5% working tolerance and ranges as the general case. Folded into T-068; the diagnostics reader is owed (`OPEN-ITEMS-PLAN.md` OI-57 (36)).
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/REMEDIATION-WORKPLAN.md:1101:  - (a) A quantity kind of presence (provided or not provided, or a count of provisions), added by data with a warrant (T-020's `add-quantity-kind`; OD-24 allows a kind to be "extended by data with a warrant"), so such a provision becomes a parameter with its own determination, lens, marker and branches. *Then:* the engine, its anchoring and agreement rules (T-059, T-068), the floor and above-floor derivation, and render's sentences meet a value that has two states and no direction of more or less accommodating on a scale; the resolver says how a direction (`base_parameters.accessibility_direction`), a bound and "best practice is the most accommodating value" read for it, or the option fails criterion 1. A count of provisions (for example one visual alarm per room) is a quantity and already fits the model; presence alone is the hard case. T-010 plans one rule of refused domains (`NON_QUANTITY_DOMAINS`, T-010 section 4 item 1: lenses, methods and bodies of law); the domains the held provision terms sit in are not among them, which the resolver confirms on the merged code.
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/REMEDIATION-WORKPLAN.md:1277:**Thirteenth set (2026-11-14).** The owner answered the four items of "Four things to see first" in `OWNER-SHEET-PLAIN.md` (`grep -n -F "Owner answers 2026-11-14 (thirteenth set)" references/project-standards.md`): (1) agreement between any two kinds of evidence counts as convergence, and convergence defines most common practice, which is not best practice (OD-43 answered by the owner; its delegated limit to the clinical and Co-1 axes superseded on contact); (2) OD-44 answered A; (3) the measurement first, and the guidebook concerns design itself, so "new or existing" and code status leave the circumstances OD-49 types (building use and interior or exterior remain); (4) provisions whose question is presence, such as hearing loops, are included, which overtakes OD-53's declination for them and registers OD-56 (how), open for a delegated, independently checked resolution. Folded into T-068, T-070, T-091, T-092, and a render note in T-037 and T-032; `OPEN-ITEMS-PLAN.md` OI-60; `DECISION-CLOSURE.md` §4 prompt 18.
